; STOCK-1 (2026-09-20) -- THE ORANGES. Talon asked for "piles of fruit in bins and crates", and
; this is where they live: one MultiMesh of 29 produce instances, generated from ShelfStock's
; arithmetic and asserted against it by StockBakeTests. Read BinMound.tscn's own header for why
; it carries NO COLLISION -- in one line, because a mound collider would delete the "hide the
; crate under a tipped bin" affordance SHELF-1's bible check closed INTERACTION S3 on, and there
; is no half-fill that keeps it.
;
; IT IS A CHILD OF THE ROOT, NOT OF Visual. Carryable._Ready looks up "Visual/MeshInstance3D" by
; NAME to clone its outline shell from, and adds the shell as a sibling inside Visual; a
; MultiMeshInstance3D in there would be a second mesh in the one place this prefab's own code
; goes looking. At the root it is invisible to all four of the collider/mesh lookups this
; prefab's header lists, and its transform is the bin's base, which is the space the mound's
; own coordinates are in.
[node name="BinMound" parent="." instance=ExtResource("3_mound")]
